{
  "description": "Views as Postgres 17 prints them (pg_get_viewdef), introspected by the gateway from a real database, each seeding literals the cloud must never see. Every case must evaluate the same on the redacted copy (the core's agreement test). Two views Postgres prints in forms pgsql-deparser can't say faithfully (a quoted \"bit\" cast, FETCH ... WITH TIES) are left out: the gateway withholds their definitions (see the core's redaction test).",
